          %h2#references References
          %p Some ideas pointing to higher symplectic groupoids were indicated in
          %ul#Severa
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavol+%C5%A0evera"}> Pavol Ševera
              ,
              %em Some title containing the words “homotopy” and “symplectic”, e.g. this one
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105080"}> arXiv:math/0105080
              ).
          %p
            Aspects of the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
            are in
          %ul#Rogers
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
              ,
              %em Higher symplectic geometry
              PhD thesis (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4068"}> arXiv:1106.4068
              )
          %p A discussion of higher symplectic geometry in a general context is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+geometric+prequantization"} Higher geometric prequantization
          %p See also section 4.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              \.
          %p
